From 704751ca6b7cc5ad3ba8720f863841588f6f0408 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: HuJK <gh@hujk.oeg>
Date: Sun, 12 Jul 2026 22:39:23 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] virtio-gpu/gunyah: gate memparcel accept on
 gunyah_guest_available()

The blob-mmap path took the Gunyah mem_accept branch whenever the host set a
non-zero gunyah_handle in the map response. On a non-Gunyah hypervisor (KVM,
gzvm, ...) or any host that leaves that field non-zero, the accept would fail
with -ENODEV and abort the mmap instead of falling back to the stock
io_remap_pfn_range path. Gate on gunyah_guest_available() (false unless the
gunyah-resource-manager DT node was found at init) so a non-Gunyah guest never
touches the memparcel path and degrades to plain virtio-gpu behaviour. No HVC
is ever issued off-Gunyah, so there is no panic risk either way.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Smu6N2o945D86k4hE1i9jr
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/virtio/virtgpu_vram.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/virtio/virtgpu_vram.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/virtio/virtgpu_vram.c
index edf042cc0ca9..bfd16e8021fc 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/virtio/virtgpu_vram.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/virtio/virtgpu_vram.c
@@ -66,7 +66,7 @@ static int virtio_gpu_vram_mmap(struct drm_gem_object *obj,
 	 * protected guest's stage-2. Accept the memparcel here (sleepable context)
 	 * so the IPA at vram_node.start becomes accessible before io_remap.
 	 */
-	if (vram->gunyah_handle && !vram->gunyah_accepted) {
+	if (gunyah_guest_available() && vram->gunyah_handle && !vram->gunyah_accepted) {
 		ret = gunyah_guest_mem_accept(vram->gunyah_handle,
 					      vram->vram_node.start,
 					      vram->vram_node.size);
